# GitHub Linguist language-statistics correction
# ffi_win.inc is generated code for the in-house Windows FFI ABI wrapper (1705 static wrapper functions, 515KB),
# and Linguist reads the .inc suffix as C++, which made the language bar report 57% C++; marking it generated keeps it out of the statistics.
internal/lang/ffi_win.inc linguist-generated=true

# The tree-sitter parser under editors/ is generated from grammar.js; keep it out of the language statistics.
editors/tree-sitter-quarklang/src/** linguist-generated=true

# Compiled artefacts: excluded from diffs
compiler/qkc binary

# The authored message tables are the input to the generated catalog in internal/i18n. Pin them to LF in
# every checkout: a CRLF working tree would otherwise put a carriage return inside a message's text on
# Windows and make the generator's output platform-dependent. (The syntax layer pins the same pattern.)
internal/i18n/source/*.tsv text eol=lf
# The generated status report and its authored inputs are compared byte for byte by the drift gate:
# pin them to LF in every checkout, or a Windows working tree checks them out CRLF and the gate fails
# on the line endings rather than on a stale report.
docs/implementation-status.md text eol=lf
spec/status/claims.tsv text eol=lf
spec/status/template.md text eol=lf

# The generated tide report is compared byte for byte by the drift gate, and its record/template are
# its inputs: pin them to LF so a Windows checkout cannot fail on line endings instead of on a stale report.
docs/tide-benchmark.md text eol=lf
spec/bench/tide.tsv text eol=lf
spec/bench/tide-template.md text eol=lf
